WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.969
NETFLIX ANIME

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:08.575
We managed to get some questions answered

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:10.910
by the production staff of Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway too!

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.114
Here I go!

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.715
Ta-da!

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.417
Hi! It’s me, N-ko!

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.818
This may seem random,

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:21.654
but have you already seen the latest in the Gundam series,

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:27.060
Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway?

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.497
Soon after being released in theaters in Japan,

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:36.336
it became the biggest hit of all Gundam movies!

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:41.007
It’s a long awaited movie for all Gundam fans!

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:45.078
Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway is streaming

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:50.350
only on Netflix outside of Japan.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:57.657
Actually, I hadn't properly watched much Gundam until now.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.759
I’m definitely interested,

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.895
but since there are so many titles,

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:06.766
I have no idea where to start.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:11.271
I was really worried I wouldn't be able to understand Hathaway,

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:16.710
having not seen the previous titles.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:23.016
But when I asked the hardcore Gundam fans at Netflix,

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:27.787
I found out that Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway can be enjoyed

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:33.526
even if you haven’t watched any of the previous Gundam titles!

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:40.834
However, if you’ve seen the previous titles, it'll be even more fun to watch!

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:46.106
I will share which Gundam titles you should watch before watching the movie,

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:52.312
and some basic information for you to fully enjoy it.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:55.782
I'm a Gundam newbie myself,

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.684
so bear with me

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:04.057
if I don’t have the details or my explanation is incorrect.

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:08.528
Let’s introduce some titles!

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:11.731
Here I go!

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:17.137
Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway is a three part series.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:22.108
The one that’s streaming right now is part one.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:25.979
It’s set in the year U.C. 0105.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:30.984
U.C. stands for Universal Century, a timeline in the Gundam series.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:36.556
When the total population on Earth went over nine billion,

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:42.295
the Earth Federation decided to move people out to space.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:47.967
That’s when the calendar year was changed to the Universal Century.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:50.804
However, only the privileged,

00:02:50.804 --> 00:02:52.806
such as high officials of the Earth Federation,

00:02:52.806 --> 00:02:58.078
or the rich, are allowed to live on Earth.

00:02:58.078 --> 00:03:01.348
In addition, the Earth Federation

00:03:01.348 --> 00:03:05.652
uses a police force called “Man Hunters”

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:08.822
to hunt down any illegal residents on Earth,

00:03:08.822 --> 00:03:13.493
and exile them back into space.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:17.964
The anti-Federation group called “Mafty”

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:22.369
takes a stand against the Earth Federation.

00:03:22.369 --> 00:03:25.972
They fight against the Earth Federation,

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:34.547
with the goal to force all humanity from Earth into outer space.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:38.218
And the leader of Mafty,

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:42.622
who goes by the name of Mafty Navue Erin,

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:46.292
is the protagonist of this movie, Hathaway Noa.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:50.930
He is the son of Bright Noa, who commanded the protagonist
and his team in the very first Gundam series,

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:58.838
and is praised as the hero of the Earth Federation in this era.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.440
When I think of Gundam,

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:04.811
I think of it as a simple robot anime,

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:08.114
but isn't this setting quite detailed?

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:13.586
During the film, Mafty, aka Hathaway, has an encounter

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:17.957
with Earth Federation officer Colonel Kenneth Sleg,

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.326
and develops a friendship with him.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:26.900
Kenneth is assigned as the commander of the Mafty Annihilation Unit.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:30.303
In other words, he’s Hathaway’s arch rival.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:35.342
Of course, Hathaway is hiding his identity from Kenneth.

00:04:35.342 --> 00:04:36.443
In addition,

00:04:36.443 --> 00:04:40.080
he meets a mysterious girl named Gigi Andalucia

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.981
around the same time he meets Kenneth.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:50.590
Hathaway is attracted to Gigi's mature yet childlike mysterious personality.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:57.731
However, Gigi uses her mysterious powers to detect that Hathaway is Mafty.

00:04:57.731 --> 00:05:02.302
Hathaway is wary, but attracted to Gigi at the same time.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:06.406
On top of that, Kenneth gets involved,

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.241
and turns it into a love triangle!

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:14.948
Suspenseful and heart-stopping relationships intermixed with friends and foes.

00:05:14.948 --> 00:05:18.485
That's another charm of Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway.

00:05:18.485 --> 00:05:28.695
Many may think of Gundam as a show about robots, mecha, and mobile suits,

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:29.562
but in reality,

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:33.166
it also has rich and deep human drama.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:35.602
It's also about the government,

00:05:35.602 --> 00:05:37.570
or about politics.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.940
It really matches the current zeitgeist.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:45.612
I think the story covers all of society.

00:05:45.612 --> 00:05:49.949
Especially with Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway,

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.885
I felt like I was on a trip.

00:05:51.885 --> 00:05:57.991
It started with a scene that made me feel like I was on a luxury cruise ship,

00:05:57.991 --> 00:06:03.797
and it takes place somewhere Japanese people would consider “abroad.”

00:06:03.797 --> 00:06:09.502
The movie gave me the feeling of being on a trip.

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:13.139
It was a beautiful movie to watch,

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:18.778
and it was an interesting title, even without any knowledge about Gundam.

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:19.746
Now,

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:21.715
speaking of the Gundam series,

00:06:21.715 --> 00:06:25.251
there are lots of titles.

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:27.220
But if we were to categorize them,

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:30.023
there are series set in the Universal Century timeline,

00:06:30.023 --> 00:06:33.526
and those that are not.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:36.062
Those are the two main categories.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:40.533
Titles set in the Universal Century timeline

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:43.803
are all connected as part of one history.

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:46.973
Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway is part of

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:51.244
the Universal Century timeline.

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:54.180
That means if you watch the past U.C. titles,

00:06:54.180 --> 00:07:00.520
you’ll know all the history leading up to Hathaway.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:04.224
You can enjoy this movie on its own,

00:07:04.224 --> 00:07:06.993
but when you find out where it stands in the history of the series,

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:11.598
it’s even more entertaining.

00:07:11.598 --> 00:07:15.969
This is one of the charms of Gundam.

00:07:15.969 --> 00:07:19.205
According to the Gundam lovers at Netflix,

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:23.543
the U.C. Gundam titles that come before Hathaway

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:26.813
are as follows.

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:28.415
"Mobile Suit Gundam"

00:07:28.415 --> 00:07:29.416
"Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam"

00:07:29.416 --> 00:07:30.417
"Mobile Suit Gundam ZZ"

00:07:30.417 --> 00:07:31.418
"Mobile Suit Gundam: Char's Counterattack"
"Mobile Suit Gundam Unicorn"

00:07:31.418 --> 00:07:32.419
"Mobile Suit Gundam Narrative"

00:07:32.419 --> 00:07:33.219
"Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway"

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:37.257
As you can see, there are many more Gundam titles

00:07:37.257 --> 00:07:40.326
prior to Hathaway.

00:07:41.261 --> 00:07:47.600
And Hathaway appears in some of them as a child.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:54.474
Now, these two shows are the ones you ought to watch
before you watch Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway.

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:57.377
The first one is Mobile Suit Gundam.

00:07:57.377 --> 00:08:00.847
It’s the very first Gundam series,

00:08:00.847 --> 00:08:05.752
and it’s also referred to as "First Gundam."

00:08:05.752 --> 00:08:09.756
It takes place in U.C. 0079.

00:08:09.756 --> 00:08:13.993
One of the space colonies, Side 3, where the immigrants live,

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:17.697
declares itself as the Principality of Zeon,

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:21.234
calling for independence from the Earth Federation.

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:29.409
This is the start of the One Year War.

00:08:29.409 --> 00:08:34.948
The protagonist Amuro Ray gets mixed up in this war.

00:08:34.948 --> 00:08:43.790
Bright Noa is the leader of Amuro’s team and the Captain of the White Base.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:47.227
He's Hathaway's father.

00:08:47.227 --> 00:08:53.500
By the way, his mother is Mirai Yashima, the helmsman of White Base.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:09:01.441
That means this is the story where Hathaway’s parent’s meet.

00:09:01.441 --> 00:09:04.244
This is the origin of the Gundam series,

00:09:04.244 --> 00:09:11.117
and the basis for the whole Universal Century timeline.

00:09:11.117 --> 00:09:14.354
So let’s start by watching this series.

00:09:14.354 --> 00:09:19.459
By the way, if you search Mobile Suit Gundam on Netflix,

00:09:19.459 --> 00:09:25.498
you might get both the TV series and the three-part movie series in some regions.

00:09:25.498 --> 00:09:31.104
But I recommend watching the movies since they're shorter.

00:09:31.104 --> 00:09:33.573
But to meet the time frame,

00:09:33.573 --> 00:09:37.777
some amazing scenes have been cut from the movie version.

00:09:37.777 --> 00:09:41.748
So if you are curious, please watch the TV series.

00:09:41.748 --> 00:09:46.653
The next one is Mobile Suit Gundam: Char's Counterattack.

00:09:46.653 --> 00:09:53.226
It was released over 30 years ago, in 1988,

00:09:53.226 --> 00:09:54.894
but Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway

00:09:54.894 --> 00:10:00.166
is a direct sequel to this movie.

00:10:00.166 --> 00:10:06.006
It involves the final battle between protagonist Amuro Ray

00:10:06.006 --> 00:10:13.513
and his rival, Char Aznable.

00:10:13.513 --> 00:10:17.951
Hathaway appears as a 13-year-old in this movie.

00:10:17.951 --> 00:10:22.889
What did Hathaway see and feel during the war?

00:10:22.889 --> 00:10:25.525
Mobile Suit Gundam: Char's Counterattack scenes are mentioned

00:10:25.525 --> 00:10:30.196
in Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway as well,

00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:31.531
so if you watch it,

00:10:31.531 --> 00:10:35.235
you’ll be able to follow the story more smoothly.

00:10:35.235 --> 00:10:37.871
The Universal Century Gundam titles,

00:10:37.871 --> 00:10:41.408
including Mobile Suit Gundam and Mobile Suit Gundam: Char's Counterattack,

00:10:41.408 --> 00:10:46.579
can all be found on Netflix.

00:10:46.579 --> 00:10:49.282
Please watch these titles

00:10:49.282 --> 00:10:51.785
before you watch Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway,

00:10:51.785 --> 00:10:53.420
and prepare yourself!

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.923
Of course, it’s all right to get hooked

00:10:56.923 --> 00:11:01.027
on other Gundam titles after you watch Hathaway too.

00:11:01.027 --> 00:11:06.232
Now, all I’ve been doing so far is talk about the storyline,

00:11:06.232 --> 00:11:09.502
but aren’t you curious about Gundam mobile suits too?

00:11:09.502 --> 00:11:13.073
I am not an expert on robots,

00:11:13.073 --> 00:11:15.942
so I haven’t mentioned them so far,

00:11:15.942 --> 00:11:21.147
but that’s one essential part of the Gundam franchise.

00:11:21.147 --> 00:11:24.784
In Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway,

00:11:24.784 --> 00:11:29.389
Xi Gundam appears as Hathaway’s Gundam.

00:11:29.389 --> 00:11:31.358
Its biggest characteristic

00:11:31.358 --> 00:11:35.362
is that it can fly freely on Earth.

00:11:35.362 --> 00:11:37.897
Because of Earth’s gravity,

00:11:37.897 --> 00:11:43.136
previous Gundam models could jump using a booster,

00:11:43.136 --> 00:11:47.607
but they were unable to fly at high speed for a long period at a time.

00:11:47.607 --> 00:11:53.546
To fly, they have to transform into waverider form like the Zeta Gundam,

00:11:53.546 --> 00:11:56.750
or to go onto a transport carrier.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.386
However, the Xi Gundam has

00:11:59.386 --> 00:12:02.689
a Minovsky Flight Unit installed,

00:12:02.689 --> 00:12:05.258
allowing it to fly freely at high speed through the air,

00:12:05.258 --> 00:12:08.995
even with gravity.

00:12:08.995 --> 00:12:12.432
The Minovsky Flight Unit is only installed

00:12:12.432 --> 00:12:14.000
in the Xi Gundam

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:18.438
and its rival machine, Penelope.

00:12:18.438 --> 00:12:25.645
You can’t blink during these two Gundams' high-speed air combat.

00:12:25.645 --> 00:12:30.550
Since this Xi Gundam can fly,

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:32.819
its straight lines are really cool.

00:12:32.819 --> 00:12:35.121
I would say that overall, it’s like...

00:12:35.121 --> 00:12:37.824
swoosh, swoosh, swoosh!

00:12:37.824 --> 00:12:41.061
I think its body design is really cool.

00:12:41.061 --> 00:12:43.663
I thought it was a very distinctive mobile suit design

00:12:43.663 --> 00:12:45.565
where you can guess it instantly

00:12:45.565 --> 00:12:49.903
if it were to appear as a silhouette.

00:12:49.903 --> 00:12:55.308
I’ve been talking about Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway

00:12:55.308 --> 00:12:59.145
and the Gundam series so far,

00:12:59.145 --> 00:13:02.215
but now I have something special!

00:13:02.849 --> 00:13:07.821
We were able to get an email interview

00:13:07.821 --> 00:13:11.324
with Ogata, the producer of the film.

00:13:11.324 --> 00:13:14.828
Thank you very much, Producer Ogata.

00:13:14.828 --> 00:13:21.634
He shared highlights and behind-the-scenes stories for a Gundam newbie like me.

00:13:21.634 --> 00:13:23.203
I would now like to share that with you.

00:13:23.203 --> 00:13:28.575
"Simply put, what kind of a girl is Gigi Andalucia?"

00:13:28.575 --> 00:13:32.012
"She seemed mature and childish at the same time."

00:13:32.012 --> 00:13:35.782
"She is hard to figure out. She truly was a femme fatale."

00:13:35.782 --> 00:13:41.688
"Please tell us the story behind building the character."

00:13:41.688 --> 00:13:47.260
"For men, Gigi is a mysterious woman"

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:50.096
"who they can never figure out."

00:13:50.096 --> 00:13:54.167
"In terms of character, she contains several characteristics of women"

00:13:54.167 --> 00:13:59.906
"that appear in the works of Yoshiyuki Tomino."

00:13:59.906 --> 00:14:03.576
"In creating the film, I couldn’t avoid Quess,"

00:14:03.576 --> 00:14:07.580
"who appeared in Mobile Suit Gundam: Char's Counterattack."

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:13.787
"She had a huge effect on creating Gigi’s character in this piece."

00:14:14.187 --> 00:14:18.291
So about what Producer Ogata said about Gigi

00:14:18.291 --> 00:14:20.927
being a mysterious being

00:14:20.927 --> 00:14:26.533
whom men can never comprehend...

00:14:26.533 --> 00:14:30.503
This really is clear when you watch the movie.

00:14:30.503 --> 00:14:36.976
The movie is mainly from Hathaway’s perspective,

00:14:36.976 --> 00:14:40.947
and so from Hathaway’s perspective, Gigi is seen as a mysterious woman,

00:14:40.947 --> 00:14:47.387
and he can’t comprehend her.

00:14:47.387 --> 00:14:50.123
It's really beautifully and well portrayed.

00:14:50.123 --> 00:14:58.131
It made me think maybe women are mysterious beings that men will never understand.

00:14:58.965 --> 00:15:04.437
"If there are any highlights from the production team side"

00:15:04.437 --> 00:15:08.808
"where fans could declare themselves as true Gundam fans"

00:15:08.808 --> 00:15:10.176
"when they notice this part in the movie, please let us know."

00:15:10.176 --> 00:15:14.280
"The cockpit in the Messer is located in its head."

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:17.250
"This is to express the fact that the Messer’s design is derived"

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:23.256
"from the Sazabi in Mobile Suit Gundam: Char's Counterattack."

00:15:23.256 --> 00:15:27.994
Gundam lovers should remember these facts!

00:15:27.994 --> 00:15:34.701
"Which Gundam title is the most popular among the production crew?"

00:15:34.701 --> 00:15:37.470
"We understand it's hard to narrow it down,"

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:42.475
"but if you have to just pick one, which one would it be?"

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:47.313
"Each member of the production crew is different,"

00:15:47.313 --> 00:15:54.521
"but many of us, including myself, love Char's Counterattack."

00:15:54.521 --> 00:16:00.193
I’m definitely planning to watch Char's Counterattack,

00:16:00.193 --> 00:16:07.634
which is closely related to Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway.

00:16:08.034 --> 00:16:11.571
"The main theme, 'Senko,' performed by Alexandros"

00:16:11.571 --> 00:16:14.074
"is such a great fit for the movie."

00:16:14.074 --> 00:16:18.745
"I felt it was part of the charm of the movie."

00:16:18.745 --> 00:16:22.082
"What kind of request did you make"

00:16:22.082 --> 00:16:24.851
"when you asked them to write the music?"

00:16:25.552 --> 00:16:30.957
"This movie is the first movie of the series,"

00:16:30.957 --> 00:16:35.195
"and the fact that it’s the brightest moment of Hathaway’s life,"

00:16:35.195 --> 00:16:39.366
"when Alexandros first offered the music,"

00:16:39.399 --> 00:16:43.670
"it sounded much heavier and darker,"

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:47.540
"so we had them change it to music"

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:52.645
"that’s up-tempo and fast, and could be used as an opening for a TV series."

00:16:52.645 --> 00:16:59.019
"For the lyrics, we requested Yohei Kawakami read the novel in detail,"

00:16:59.019 --> 00:17:04.290
"and come up with a theme song that went along with Hathaway’s life."

00:17:04.891 --> 00:17:09.162
"Their agent is a huge Gundam fan,"

00:17:09.162 --> 00:17:12.032
"and their label RX-Records' "RX","

00:17:12.032 --> 00:17:13.867
"came from Gundam."

00:17:13.867 --> 00:17:18.471
"They happily accepted our offer"

00:17:18.471 --> 00:17:22.909
"and also participated in several promotions."

00:17:22.909 --> 00:17:29.482
That music could certainly be an opening song for a TV series.

00:17:29.482 --> 00:17:31.184
It was very refreshing.

00:17:31.184 --> 00:17:37.123
I would also like to hear the heavier and darker music.

00:17:37.123 --> 00:17:43.196
Thank you for taking the time to answer all the questions despite your busy schedule.

00:17:43.196 --> 00:17:50.136
Now, before seeing Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway,

00:17:50.136 --> 00:17:56.876
I was thinking that Gundam seemed hard to comprehend and get into,

00:17:56.876 --> 00:18:00.246
but the more I learn about it, the more it opens my eyes.

00:18:00.246 --> 00:18:05.785
I now want to watch more Gundam titles!

00:18:05.785 --> 00:18:11.524
How about all Gundam fans as well as non-Gundam fans

00:18:11.524 --> 00:18:17.097
watch Mobile Suit Gundam Hathaway?

00:18:17.097 --> 00:18:20.133
It’s a three-part series,

00:18:20.133 --> 00:18:26.306
so I can’t wait to watch its sequels, part two and part three!

00:18:26.306 --> 00:18:32.112
I would be so happy if you could write your opinion in the comments section!

00:18:32.112 --> 00:18:36.750
I’ll see you again in the next video!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:38.451
See you!

